            <ArticleTitle>Ischiadic nerve entrapment by an extra- and intrapelvic lipoma: a rare cause of sciatica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>532-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-year-old woman had persistent left-sided ischialgia. After several years, a left-sided subgluteal mass extended to the pelvis. Computed tomography (CT) disclosed a large subgluteal and intrapelvic lipoma. Symptoms were relieved by excision of the tumor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
